  "body": "# CoAkka Runtime 1.4.0\n\nRuntime `1.4.0` aligns the public native C ABI, language connectors, framework\nadapters, documentation, and auditable native consumer tests around source\nsnapshot `2cee86bf89f38725aa763bb3abd96b64a904875d`.\n\n## Artifact Identity\n\n- Native generation: `1.4.0+2cee86bf`\n- Connector generation: `1.4.0+2cee86bf-ec4902c`\n- Python package projection: `1.4.5` from connector `77c9db8`\n- npm package projection: `1.4.5` from connector `2c0c598`\n- NuGet package projection: `1.4.6` from connector `693f122`\n- Maven generation: `1.4.0-g2cee86bf-ec4902c`\n- Native platforms: Linux ARM64, macOS ARM64, and Windows x86-64\n- Public C exports: 101 on every included native platform\n\nEach release directory contains a machine-readable manifest and\n`SHA256SUMS`. The root [`artifacts/public-artifacts.tsv`](../../artifacts/public-artifacts.tsv)\nis the authoritative download ledger.\n\n## Connector Surface\n\nThe release includes JVM, Spring Boot, Quarkus, Node.js, Bun, Electron,\nPython, Go, C#, Rust, Swift, Tauri, Mojo, and Zig artifacts. Every connector\nuses the core capability and configuration contract for startup connection\nstrategy, structured atomic apply results, and TLS/mTLS credential reload.\n\nConnection strategy, TLS/mTLS, and failure semantics are documented in the\n[connection strategy guide](../connection-strategies.md),\n[TLS/mTLS guide](../tls-and-mtls.md), and\n[troubleshooting guide](../troubleshooting.md).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Native libraries pass dependency and exact 101-export checks.\n- The JVM JAR loads its embedded runtime and reports version `1.4.0`, source\n  snapshot `2cee86bf`, and capability mask `221`.\n- Language package dry-runs install or unpack into clean consumers and execute\n  their platform-appropriate smoke tests.\n- The root [`runtime-test/`](../../runtime-test/README.md) covers request/reply,\n  bounded admission, all four connection strategies, structured rejection,\n  static analysis, and consumer-side ASan/UBSan controls.\n- Linux ARM64 CI builds that public harness against the exact released 1.4.0\n  archive, then runs both the workload and four-mode connection-strategy\n  executables with ASan/UBSan. This instruments the public consumer source, not\n  the closed runtime binary.\n- On macOS ARM64, the public C11 harness passes static analysis across all nine\n  translation units, request/reply `64/64`, connection strategy `4/4`, and\n  both consumer-side ASan/UBSan executables with Homebrew LLVM 22.1.5. The\n  troubleshooting guide records the AppleClang sanitizer-runtime stall that\n  can occur before `main` on affected hosts.\n- TLS/mTLS conformance covers all four connection strategies; failed\n  credential reload preserves the active configuration.\n- `coakka-client` and `coakka-runtime-inspect` 1.4.0 macOS ARM64 bundles pass\n  unpacked dependency and command smokes. Linux and Windows tool archives keep\n  their separately recorded prior generations until matching native builds are\n  available.\n\n## Platform Trust\n\nThe 1.4.0 files are distributed without publisher signing. SHA-256 verification\nis required, and users may apply their own platform signing. OS-specific trust,\ndependency, and loader guidance is in\n[troubleshooting](../troubleshooting.md).\n\n## License\n\nCoAkka Public Artifact License 1.1 applies to this release and supersedes an\nembedded copy of version 1.0. It permits royalty-free production, internal\nbusiness, commercial application, customer distribution, and SaaS use when\nCoAkka is an internal component. A separate agreement is required for a\nManaged CoAkka Service or an offering whose primary or substantial value is\nCoAkka itself. This license clarification does not change artifact bytes,\nchecksums, signing status, or runtime capabilities.\n\nPackage-manager registry publication is tracked independently from this\nartifact mirror. A package coordinate is listed as current only after the\nregistry itself serves that exact version.\n\nThe public Go module and SwiftPM package are tagged and released at `v1.4.0`:\n\n- `github.com/phuong-tran/coakka-runtime-go@v1.4.0`\n- `https://github.com/phuong-tran/coakka-runtime-swift.git`, exact `1.4.0`\n\nThe PyPI runtime lane is registry-verified at\n`coakka-v2-connector==1.4.5`, the npm runtime lanes are registry-verified at\n`coakka-v2-connector-{node,bun,electron}@1.4.5`, and the NuGet runtime lane is\nregistry-verified at `CoAkka.Runtime==1.4.6`. All use native generation\n`1.4.0+2cee86bf`. The original 1.4.0 package files remain downloadable from\nthis artifact release alongside the immutable package-manager projections.\n",
